    yalaaiNote: 'Yala AI is a Pro feature. To answer you it processes your financial context with OpenAI, only when you turn it on. More details in our Privacy Policy.',
    yalaaiBadge: 'Pro',
    groupsTitle: 'Who owes whom? Yala knows.',
    groupsBullet1: 'Create a group for a trip, the house, or anything you like.',
    groupsBullet2: 'Record who paid what and Yala works out the balances for you.',
    groupsBadge: 'Beta',
    featureAITitle: 'Yala AI · Pro',
    featureAIDesc: 'Your financial assistant. Ask, log, and understand your month.',
    featureGroupsTitle: 'Groups · Beta',
    featureGroupsDesc: 'Split expenses with anyone and Yala works out who owes whom.',
    pricingPro8: 'Yala AI: your financial assistant',
    galleryTitle: 'Inside Yala',
    gallerySubtitle: 'A look at the app, screen by screen.',
    faq8Q: 'What data does Yala AI use?',
    faq8A: 'When you ask it something or have it log an expense, Yala AI sends OpenAI a summary of your financial situation (account balances and names, totals by category, frequent merchants, tags, budgets, and recurring payments) to generate the response. It only happens when you turn it on and give your consent, and, under OpenAI\'s API policy, it does not use this data to train its models. It is a Pro feature.',
    faq9Q: 'Are Groups private?',
    faq9A: 'A group\'s expenses and balances are only seen by its members. To use Groups you sign in with Apple or Google, and the group is stored on Yala\'s servers, with the name, aliases, amounts and notes encrypted with a key held by our server. Your email isn\'t shared with the group, neither is your data outside it, and you can leave a group whenever you want. Groups is in Beta.',
    privacyGroupsTitle: '5. Groups and shared expenses',
    privacyGroupsText: 'To use Groups you sign in with Apple or Google, even if your personal data stays in your iCloud. Groups live on Yala\'s servers so all members see the same expenses, up to date.\n\n• **What\'s stored:** the group\'s name, icon and currency, each member\'s alias, expenses with their amount, description, date, category and note, how each expense is split, and settlements.\n• **How it\'s protected:** the group name, aliases, amounts, descriptions and notes are stored encrypted with a key held by our server. It isn\'t end-to-end encryption: our server can decrypt them so the group works.\n• **Who sees it:** the group\'s members. Your email isn\'t shared with the group, and neither are your finances outside it.\n• **Invitations:** an invite link carries the group\'s name, icon and color, the aliases of up to five members and the inviter\'s, to show a preview. Anyone with the link sees that data and can join while it\'s valid (7 days).\n• **Notifications:** while you\'re signed in, we store your device\'s notification token to tell you about changes in your groups. Apple delivers the notification, and it carries no amounts or names.\n• **When you leave a group** you stop seeing it, but the expenses you added stay in the group for the others.\n\nIf you used Groups in earlier versions of Yala, those older groups were shared through iCloud, using Apple\'s CloudKit Sharing.',
    termsGroupsTitle: '6. Groups and shared content (Beta)',
    termsGroupsText: 'Groups lets you share expenses with other people and requires you to sign in with Apple or Google. You\'re responsible for the content you share and for the people you invite: anyone who receives an invite link can see the group\'s preview and join while the link is valid. The other members can see the expenses, balances and your alias within the group. If you leave the group or delete your account, the expenses you added stay in the group (under "Deleted user" if you delete your account). Groups is in Beta: balance calculations are indicative and the feature may contain errors. We\'re not responsible for disputes between members or for the accuracy of shared data.',

